OL,3,GNEWSAAvian botulism 'new norm' for
OL,4,Anature reserves
OL,5,
OL,6,FA conservation group has warned that
OL,7,Favian botulism outbreaks will become
OL,8,Fmore common due to climate change after
OL,9,Fmore than a hundred birds died in East
OL,10,FSussex.
OL,12,FThe birds died after a suspected
OL,13,Foutbreak of the disease at Rye Harbour
OL,14,FNature Reserve, according to Sussex
OL,15,FWildlife Trust.
OL,17,FThe charity's head of nature reserves,
OL,18,FJamie Parsons, said that as heatwaves
OL,19,Fand droughts become more common, "more
OL,20,Foutbreaks are going to come along with
OL,21,Fthem".
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
